@startuml
title Every throw ends in the navigator — a tool in the middle re-raises, never swallows\n(the one authored raise that does not: ModelRetry, which ends in the pydantic-ai library)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

participant "UniversalNavigator\n(or UniversalNavigatorProxy)" as UN
participant "render ledger\n(owned by the navigator)" as RL
participant "Tool A" as A
participant "Tool B" as B
participant "Tool C" as C
participant "pydantic-ai\n(library frame)" as PA

== The re-raise chain: a throw travels up the may_call graph ==

UN -> A : dispatch
activate A
A -> B : may_call (declared, acyclic)
activate B
B -> C : may_call
activate C
C -->> B : throw (ChatHealthyException, mode discriminator)
deactivate C
note right of B #f9efef
  re-raises — never catches,
  never logs. A bare re-raise
  authors nothing.
end note
B -->> A : re-raised
deactivate B
A -->> UN : re-raised
deactivate A

note over UN #eef6f5
  The catch site. The navigator is the client to
  every server and service, so it — not a tool in
  the middle — catches, classifies the mode, logs
  (with timings, severity matched to impact), and
  answers. An external exception keeps its native
  type until a boundary converts it to a
  ChatHealthyException carrying the original. A
  recursion guard bounds the may_call depth so a
  cycle cannot run.
end note

== The render ledger raises too — and it also ends in the navigator ==

UN -> RL : reconcile page
activate RL
note right of RL #f9efef
  A page reconciles when every
  required_member closes OR
  completeness.render_timeout_seconds
  expires. A page-merge conflict or a
  dead required member raises.
end note
RL -->> UN : raised (instrumented)
deactivate RL

== The one carve-out: ModelRetry does NOT reach the navigator ==

note over A, PA #fdf6ec
  A function registered as a pydantic-ai @output_validator
  may raise ModelRetry to reject a model answer. It is the
  library's callback protocol, not an authored ChatHealthy
  exception: pydantic-ai catches it in its own frame to ask
  the model again. The object never enters ChatHealthy code
  and no navigator catch site ever sees it.
end note
A -> PA : run (output_validator registered)
activate A
activate PA
PA -->> A : (validator raises ModelRetry — caught by PA, retried)
deactivate PA
A -->> UN : normal result or a ChatHealthyException (never ModelRetry)
deactivate A
@enduml
